        <definition>typedef int(*) NDXLNetworkCallback(NDXLNetwork *_Network, double _Time, void *_Params)</definition>
        <argsstring>(NDXLNetwork *_Network, double _Time, void *_Params)</argsstring>
        <name>NDXLNetworkCallback</name>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Network callback function. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Defines a user-supplied discrete callback that is invoked during network simulation.</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">_Network</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Pointer to the network being simulated.</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">_Time</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Current local simulation time of the network.</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">_Params</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>User-defined parameters associated with the network.</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>Integer indicating callback success (zero) or failure (any nonzero value).</para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="note"><para>If this function returns a nonzero value during simulation, NDXL terminates the simulation, and internally raises a <ref refid="group__ndxl__err_1ga47f4eed5c635910039ece338f536b88a" kindref="member">NDXL_SIM_ERR</ref>. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
